## Why This Is Asked
This question tests mastery of maintaining order statistics with dynamic updates, handling duplicates efficiently, and implementing lazy deletion—all while achieving O(log n) time complexity.

## Key Concepts
- **Two heaps for median maintenance**: A max-heap stores the lower half, while a min-heap stores the upper half, allowing O(1) median retrieval
- **Duplicate handling**: Store actual values in heaps with a frequency counter map to track occurrences
- **Lazy deletion**: Defer removals by updating a delayed-delete map; prune elements lazily when they surface at heap tops to achieve O(log n) amortized erase

## Code Example
```python
import heapq

class DualHeap:
    def __init__(self):
        self.small = []  # max-heap (store negatives)
        self.large = []  # min-heap
        self.delayed = {}  # lazy deletion map
        self.small_size = 0
        self.large_size = 0

    def prune(self, heap):
        while heap:
            num = -heap[0] if heap is self.small else heap[0]
            if self.delayed.get(num, 0) > 0:
                heapq.heappop(heap)
                self.delayed[num] -= 1
                if self.delayed[num] == 0:
                    del self.delayed[num]
            else:
                break

    def rebalance(self):
        if self.small_size > self.large_size + 1:
            val = -heapq.heappop(self.small)
            self.small_size -= 1
            heapq.heappush(self.large, val)
            self.large_size += 1
        elif self.large_size > self.small_size + 1:
            val = heapq.heappop(self.large)
            self.large_size -= 1
            heapq.heappush(self.small, -val)
            self.small_size += 1

    def insert(self, num):
        if not self.small or num <= -self.small[0]:
            heapq.heappush(self.small, -num)
            self.small_size += 1
        else:
            heapq.heappush(self.large, num)
            self.large_size += 1
        self.rebalance()

    def erase(self, num):
        self.delayed[num] = self.delayed.get(num, 0) + 1
        if num <= -self.small[0]:
            self.small_size -= 1
        else:
            self.large_size -= 1
        self.rebalance()

    def getMedian(self):
        if self.small_size > self.large_size:
            self.prune(self.small)
            return -self.small[0]
        elif self.large_size > self.small_size:
            self.prune(self.large)
            return self.large[0]
        return (-self.small[0] + self.large[0]) / 2
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a dynamic, frequency-based data structure for text streams, common in search, analytics, and logs.

## Key Concepts
- Dual-map design: word→freq and freq→ordered words
- Efficient updates by relocating words between buckets
- Tie-breaking by lexicographic order
- Corner cases: zero counts, topK when fewer distinct words

## Code Example
```javascript
class WordFreqDS {
  constructor() {
    this.counts = new Map();
    this.buckets = new Map(); // freq -> Set<string>
  }
  _ensureBucket(freq) {
    if (!this.buckets.has(freq)) this.buckets.set(freq, new Set());
  }
  addWord(word) {
    const prev = this.counts.get(word) || 0;
    if (prev > 0) this.buckets.get(prev).delete(word);
    const next = prev + 1;
    this.counts.set(word, next);
    this._ensureBucket(next);
    this.buckets.get(next).add(word);
  }
  eraseWord(word) {
    const prev = this.counts.get(word);
    if (!prev) return;
    this.buckets.get(prev).delete(word);
    const next = prev - 1;
    if (next === 0) {
      this.counts.delete(word);
      return;
    }
    this.counts.set(word, next);
    this._ensureBucket(next);
    this.buckets.get(next).add(word);
  }
  getFrequency(word) {
    return this.counts.get(word) || 0;
  }
  topKWords(n) {
    const freqs = Array.from(this.buckets.keys()).sort((a,b)=>b-a);
    const res = [];
    for (const freq of freqs) {
      const words = Array.from(this.buckets.get(freq)).sort();
      for (const w of words) {
        res.push(w);
        if (res.length === n) return res;
      }
    }
    return res;
  }
}
```

